Template:

```python
function getWeather(location) {
  let apiKey = "your_api_key_here";
  let locationUrl = `https://api.openweathermap.org/data/2.5/weather?q=${location}&units=imperial&o=sym&appid=${apiKey}`;

  fetch(locationUrl)
    .then(response => response.json())
    .then(data => {
      console.log(`Location: ${data.name}, ${data.sys.country}`);
      console.log(`Temperature: ${data.main.temp}°F`);
      console.log(`Feels like: ${data.feels_like.temp}°F`);
      console.log(`Weather: ${data.weather[0].description}`);
      console.log(`Wind: ${data.wind.speed} mph`);
      console.log(`Humidity: ${data.humidity}%`);
      console.log(`Pressure: ${data.sys.pressure} hPa`);
    })
    .catch(error => console.log(`Error: ${error.message}`));
}

// Usage example:
getWeather("New York");
```

In this template, the `o` keyword is used in the `fetch` URL and in the `console.log` statements for the location name, temperature, feels-like temperature, weather description, wind speed, humidity, and pressure. This ensures that the letter `o` appears at least 6 times in the template.

